# Delivery workflow

- For nontrivial work, state the user-visible goal, acceptance criteria,
  constraints, and non-goals before editing.
- Inspect existing code, tests, rules, skills, and relevant MCP tools before
  assuming behavior is missing.
- Keep changes narrowly scoped; record adjacent issues instead of silently
  expanding the task.
- Use Laravel Boost for version-aware Laravel documentation and application
  inspection when relevant.
- Prefer tests that assert externally observable behavior.
- Run the narrowest relevant check while iterating and `./scripts/verify.sh`
  before completion.
- Treat test, lint, type, build, route, or migration failures as blockers unless
  they are proven pre-existing and reported clearly.
- Do not commit, push, merge, deploy, access production, or install/authenticate
  tools without explicit user approval.
